    markdown::tests::a_very_long_word_does_not_keep_its_rows_live_or_cost_more_than_its_length

[break] a-long-words-first-word-runs-past-its-row
rule: The first word of a row ends at the row's end when the word goes on past it, so a mark later in a long word does not hold the rows before it.
